  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nBy Friday, drier conditions are forecast to push across the local \narea throughout the day with limited shower activity across the \ncoastal plains where activity is favored. The upper level high moves \nback into our area over the weekend to limit any shower activity. An \nupper level disturbance is forecast to move westward across the Gulf \nstates over the weekend into early next week. Latest guidance \nshowing this feature slowing and staying across the Gulf northern \nwater and then moving to the southwest as an inverted trough. So, \nconfidence is low as far as how much rain will get next week. \nHowever, our confidence is moderate to high when it comes to high \ntemperatures remaining above normal climate values.",
